{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar","id":39849,"title":"Little gods of japan and similar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T00:59:42-08:00","id":39849,"title":"Little gods of japan and similar","content":"If memory serves, Essence is 'flavored' by acts and objects, and spirits influence the mortal world so that certain things happen to generate more of whatever particular kind of Essence they feed on to grow more powerful.<br /> <br /> But a country like Japan is chock-full of shrines to various gods and spirits. Let's assume that being the WoD, these are real spirits with numina and the standard spirit behavior, and the duties of various priests somehow help keep spirits from running amok.<br /> <br /> So how do offerings of, say, burning incense convince a storm-spirit not to make a storm? Burning incense doesn't make storm-essence, so how can it substitute from what the spirit would get after manipulating the weather? Do acts of devotion create a more 'generic' kind of essence that spirits can feed on? Does it fulfill some kind of Ban, or agreement?<br /> <br /> And how the hell would a group of werewolves deal with a spirit in a highly-religious area with possibly hundreds of mortals feeding it essence every month?<br /> <br /> My only thought is that werewolves and kinfolk must personally run all the biggest shrines to keep everything working properly. <br /> <br /> (which is a slightly hilarious thought: running Werewolf - The Anime. &quot;Spirit, you have overstepped your bounds! In the name of the moon, I will punish you!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T04:23:39-08:00","id":39903,"title":"","content":"I would probably say that what the shinto priests do is that they are preforming magical rituals designed to influence or control spirits one way or another, they just don't really know what its all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T07:39:28-08:00","id":39973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar#post39849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do offerings of, say, burning incense convince a storm-spirit not to make a storm? Burning incense doesn't make storm-essence, so how can it substitute from what the spirit would get after manipulating the weather? Do acts of devotion create a more 'generic' kind of essence that spirits can feed on? Does it fulfill some kind of Ban, or agreement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any of those are possible, another possibility is that Spirits in Japan have been shaped by this so that most of them have Influce (Devotion) or similar and can feed specifically on worship. Though my favorite is that rituals honoring a specific spirit or type of spirit can shape the Essence appropriately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar#post39849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only thought is that werewolves and kinfolk must personally run all the biggest shrines to keep everything working properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Mortals are perfectly capable of doing stuff like that. Maybe not as well as a were, but they outnumber them a few million to one so they can afford to split the load a little.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:22:07-08:00","id":40025,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's really no reason to think that burning incense doesn't work on storm spirits. One of the examples in the corebook is a spirit of disease whose ban is the rue herb, which is only vaguely medicinal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:51:47-08:00","id":40039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar?p=40025#post40025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's really no reason to think that burning incense doesn't work on storm spirits. One of the examples in the corebook is a spirit of disease whose ban is the rue herb, which is only vaguely medicinal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, virtually any spirit capable of having appreciable influence over storms is going to be complex enough that its susceptible metaphysics can draw from things other than storms, to say nothing of the chicken-and-egg relationship between Earth and Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T10:03:53-08:00","id":40044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar?p=40039#post40039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, virtually any spirit capable of having appreciable influence over storms is going to be complex enough that its susceptible metaphysics can draw from things other than storms, to say nothing of the chicken-and-egg relationship between Earth and Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. For all we know, someone could sacrifice a chicken to gain influence over a dinosaur spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:09:52-08:00","id":40240,"title":"","content":"And that's not even getting into the political shenanigans broods and domains can wind up with \u2014 maybe you're actually burning incense to appease a spirit who can petition a storm-spirit for clemency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:24:16-08:00","id":40250,"title":"","content":"There is still the danger and wild element of the Shadow. There are certainly dark spirits that the priests ward against and otherwise anger. They have likely evolved ways to prey on the &quot;spoiled&quot; and potentially lazy spirits that are directly cared for by mortals. The supported spirits become somewhere between a primary producer and a herded animal, while the unsupported ones could become their predators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:44:52-08:00","id":40428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar?p=39973#post39973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any of those are possible, another possibility is that Spirits in Japan have been shaped by this so that most of them have Influce (Devotion) or similar and can feed specifically on worship. Though my favorite is that rituals honoring a specific spirit or type of spirit can shape the Essence appropriately.<br /> <br /> Why? Mortals are perfectly capable of doing stuff like that. Maybe not as well as a were, but they outnumber them a few million to one so they can afford to split the load a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not really a few million to one in the NWOD, as Werewolves number in the Hundreds of thousands, and Wolf Blooded are in the Millions, that makes it more like a thousand to one.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I was always found of the idea that proper ritual, particularly with sacrifice can generate essence for proper spirits. Particularly in areas steeped in that tradition. Its like they make proper resonant essence.<br /> <br /> But ah well it works with ghosts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T09:38:52-08:00","id":40534,"title":"","content":"All this makes me think that a Werewolf game set in Japan could have a lot of unique plot possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:12:34-08:00","id":41021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/39849-little-gods-of-japan-and-similar?p=40428#post40428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I was always found of the idea that proper ritual, particularly with sacrifice can generate essence for proper spirits. Particularly in areas steeped in that tradition. Its like they make proper resonant essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The section on spirit cults in Blasphemies played up the you-are-what-you-eat angle, suggesting that spirits who make use of a cult will often come to believe they really are what they purport to be. In the case of the kami and similarly extensive animist systems, this could lead to a whole pantheon of such spirits - in the case of the OP's storm spirit example, it might act like and perceived as a nature spirit, even by itself, but in Werewolf terms &quot;really&quot; be a conceptual of authority, with a flavour of authority over weather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:20:01-08:00","id":41185,"title":"","content":"Also, lest it be forgotten, Japan's Shadow exhibits a particular flavor of weirdness:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Yokai in Japan&quot; sidebar (Lodges: The Splintered)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When categorizing the spirits or other creatures of Japan, it is worth noting a few particular characteristics. First, they are all bound to what may be a labyrinth of manners and propriety; Forsaken are expected to act a certain way, make the proper gestures and bows, and commit to the most graceful course of conversation. Second, most of the time the spirits seem calm and even-mannered, but they are all given to bouts of inexplicable violence and madness. This seems emblematic of some kind of powerful repression or ancient wound. Third, the spirit choirs often have somewhat inexplicable hierarchies. The kitsune, or fox-spirits, seem oddly servile to wind spirits and other air elementals. Similarly weird, some spirit hierarchies seem to include yurei (or ghosts). While departed spirits cannot cross over to the Shadow and exist only in Twilight, the Forsaken often find spirits and ghosts communing in various inexplicable ceremonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T06:34:01-08:00","id":57382,"title":"","content":"Actually, the whole Shintoist belief system and the wealth of Japanese supersititions and folktales is a very fine foundation for any kind of spirits.<br /> The wrold of darkness books seem more fond of not really building on real world myths (but rather saying things like: &quot;that true fae / spirit&quot; thinks of himself as this and that god after so many years), but really, just taking those stories with their many permutations &quot;at face value&quot; creates very interesting chronicles.<br /> Rather than pressing real world animist belief systems into the ideas of Werewolf the Forsaken, I think the reverse, using those ideas as a basis of the shadow and the spirits is rather worthwhile.<br /> Japanese media had centuries of using those ideas, make use of that experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}